@page "/forgot-password"
@using System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations
@using JiranisokoTech.Infrastructure.Identity
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.RateLimiting
@layout BareLayout
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]
@attribute [EnableRateLimiting(RecoveryLimits.Limit)]
@inject UserAdministration Administration
@inject NavigationManager Navigation

@*
    Anonymous, necessarily. The one person who needs this page is the one person who cannot
    sign in to reach it, and until now there was no page at all — an administrator had to
    issue a link by hand, which is fine on the afternoon the system is installed and useless
    at seven on a Sunday evening.

    There is no separate email-verification flow and there deliberately never was. The link
    this page sends is the verification: following it is what sets EmailConfirmed, because
    having a link that was posted to an address is the only evidence of that address anybody
    ever has. A second flow that mailed a second link to prove the same thing would be
    ceremony.
*@

<PageTitle>Forgotten your password — Jiranisoko Delivery</PageTitle>

<h1>Forgotten your password</h1>

@if (Said)
{
    @*
        The same sentence whether or not the address has an account, and the same quiet
        colour. This page must not be usable as a way of testing a list of addresses against
        this firm's staff, so nothing on it may differ — and the colour is part of that: a
        green "sent" tells somebody who only takes in the colour that a letter is on its way,
        so they wait instead of asking an administrator, when there may be no account at all.
    *@
    <p class="signin__said" role="status">
        If that address has an account here, a link to choose a new password is on its way to
        it. It works once, and your current password keeps working until you use it.
    </p>

    <p class="signin__note">
        Nothing arrived after a few minutes? The address may not be the one your account was
        opened with. An administrator can tell you which it is.
    </p>
}
else
{
    <p class="signin__note">
        Type the address your account was opened with and we will send a link to choose a new
        password.
    </p>

    <EditForm Model="Input" method="post" OnValidSubmit="Ask" FormName="forgot-password"
              class="signin__form">
        <DataAnnotationsValidator />

        <label class="signin__field">
            <span>Email</span>
            <InputText @bind-Value="Input.Email" type="email" autocomplete="email" />
            <ValidationMessage For="() => Input.Email" />
        </label>

        <button type="submit">Send the link</button>
    </EditForm>
}

<p class="signin__note"><a href="/sign-in">Back to signing in</a></p>

@code {
    private AskInput _input = new();

    [SupplyParameterFromForm]
    private AskInput Input
    {
        get => _input;
        set => _input = value ?? new AskInput();
    }

    [CascadingParameter]
    private HttpContext? Request { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Whether the form has been posted, whatever came of it.</summary>
    private bool Said { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Ask, and say the same thing regardless.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// There is no try/catch and no refusal path, because the service returns nothing and
    /// throws nothing — every outcome, including a mail server that is down, is swallowed
    /// there so that this page cannot behave differently for an address that exists.
    /// </remarks>
    private async Task Ask()
    {
        await Administration.AskForARecoveryLinkAsync(
            Input.Email,
            Navigation.BaseUri,
            Request?.Connection.RemoteIpAddress?.ToString(),
            Request?.Request.Headers.UserAgent.ToString());

        Said = true;
    }

    private sealed class AskInput
    {
        [Required(ErrorMessage = "The address your account was opened with.")]
        [EmailAddress(ErrorMessage = "That does not look like an email address.")]
        [StringLength(255)]
        public string Email { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    }
}
